      "A stable total can hide a growing tail. Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. Choose the sample from the export before the meeting. A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. The revalidation tracking record should let a second reviewer rebuild the decision from the source document and the reviewer note. Outsourced Billing Services keeps the revalidation tracking source, reviewer, and decision date together in the enrollment file so a later check does not depend on memory.",
      "## Review and next action",
      "Label the request record and the source document with their versions so a later reviewer can tell a stale extract from a current one. Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. Keep the source reference and the coded value in the same row. A clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. The revalidation tracking reviewer records the close entry, the owner, and the next action in one place. For this revalidation tracking case, Outsourced Billing Services asks the billing specialist to write the open question and the named approver before the claim moves.",
      "Make the handoff readable by the next shift and the next auditor. Keep the original request so a later correction does not erase the reason for the work. Avoid a private second version in a personal document. Do not let a deadline expand a role beyond its written limit. A revalidation tracking exception keeps the close entry attached and routes the question to the billing manager. For this revalidation tracking case, Outsourced Billing Services asks the billing specialist to write the open question and the named approver before the claim moves.",
      "## Sources and review limits",
      "The sources below describe the billing, privacy, and recordkeeping context for this protocol, not a result for this sample. The review compares [the telehealth workflow](/blog/check-a-claim-s-place-of-service-against-the-encounter-type) and [the credentialing review](/blog/review-a-payer-timely-filing-limit-before-submission) with this measurement. Each reference is checked against the publisher page on the observation date and kept beside the working file. Findings remain local operational evidence and do not replace a coding, compliance, or contract review. See [CMS: Medicare Claims Processing Manual](https://www.cms.gov/regulations-and-guidance/guidance/manuals/internet-only-manuals-ioms-items/cms018912), [CMS: National Correct Coding Initiative](https://www.cms.gov/medicare/coding-billing/national-correct-coding-initiative-ncci-edits), and [GAO Green Book](https://www.gao.gov/products/gao-14-704g) for the governing context."
